  "body": "## What\n\nEvery native picker (Open, Model, Save, Save As, Post, machine/post/theme picks) could\nopen **behind** the CamCraft window: the rfd dialog was created without an owner, and the\nshell never asked for the foreground. A dialog opened right after launch — when the app was\nstarted from a terminal or a script — was the worst case: the shell itself was not the\nforeground window, so neither it nor its dialog was visible.\n\nReproduced on Windows 11 at 125 % scaling with the v0.18.0 release build: launch the app,\npress Ctrl+O, and the `#32770` \"Open\" dialog exists but sits under the shell.\n\n## Why\n\n`crates/ui/src/file_dialog.rs` built `rfd::FileDialog` with title/filters/directory only —\n`set_parent` was never called, so Windows had no owner to keep the dialog above. The shell\nalso never called `focus_window`, so a launch from a terminal left the app behind it, and an\nowned dialog follows its owner's place in the z-order.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The shell asks for the foreground once, after the window is created.\n- Every native picker is owned by the shell window, and the owner is raised just before the\n  dialog opens.\n- The GPU refusal `MessageDialog` is owned too.\n- Hand-checked: launch from a terminal, first Ctrl+O, the dialog is visible in front; repeat\n  for Save and Model.\n\nNative dialog ownership has no headless test: rfd modals are hand-test-only in this repo\n(`egui_app/tests.rs` says so), so the evidence is the hand check plus the z-order probe.\n",
